  <p>Republic and later marks were copied as readily as imperial ones: painters’ signatures on plaques in particular are often added to later work. A mark sets the earliest a piece can be, rarely the latest. For imperial reign marks, see <a href="/marks/chinese-reign-marks">reign marks</a>; for symbols and words of praise, <a href="/marks/chinese/other-marks">other marks</a>.</p>
